      content:
          '- **SCI History**: T8 ASIA A complete paraplegia from MVC 4 years ago. Surgically stabilized T7-T9 posterior fusion. Neurologically stable. Independent manual wheelchair user. Drives with hand controls.\n- **Pregnancy Details**: G1P0 at 20 weeks. Planned pregnancy with fertility specialist consultation pre-conception. IVF was not needed — conceived naturally. Prenatal labs and anatomy scan normal. Fetus growing appropriately.\n- **Current SCI Management**: Neurogenic bladder — CIC every 4-6 hours (will need to increase frequency as uterus grows). Neurogenic bowel — digital stimulation program every other day. Skin — no history of pressure injuries. No spasticity issues.\n- **SCI-Specific Pregnancy Concerns**:\n  - **Autonomic dysreflexia**: T8 level — at risk for AD (T6 and above is classic, but some T7-T8 patients can experience AD). Uterine contractions are a potent trigger for AD.\n  - **UTIs**: Increased risk during pregnancy due to urinary stasis, increased progesterone (ureteral dilation), and CIC.\n  - **Pressure injuries**: Weight gain and altered sitting posture change pressure distribution. Wheelchair cushion may need reassessment.\n  - **DVT**: Already elevated risk from SCI; pregnancy further increases risk.\n  - **Respiratory**: T8 — respiratory function generally adequate but growing uterus may compromise diaphragmatic excursion.\n  - **Labor detection**: She will not feel uterine contractions below T8. Must rely on other signs (uterine palpation, abdominal tightening, increased spasticity, AD symptoms).\n- **Pre-pregnancy planning**: Met with maternal-fetal medicine (MFM) specialist and PM&R before conceiving. Stopped oxybutynin (pregnancy category C). Adjusted bowel medications. Folic acid supplementation started pre-conception.\n- **Psychosocial**: Married 3 years. Husband is supportive and enthusiastic about the baby. Patient works part-time as a graphic designer (remote). Mother-in-law lives nearby and has been involved but increasingly critical about the pregnancy.\n- **PMH**: No other medical history besides SCI.\n- **Medications**: Prenatal vitamins, iron supplement, docusate 100 mg BID. Stopped gabapentin and oxybutynin pre-conception.',
