          '**Vitals**: BP 102/64 mmHg (normal for SCI — low baseline), HR 82 bpm, RR 16, SpO2 99% on RA, Temp 36.8C, Weight 62 kg (pre-pregnancy 56 kg), BMI 23.\n\n**General**: Alert, pleasant female in manual wheelchair. Visible 20-week pregnant abdomen. Appears healthy and well-nourished. Good affect. Mother-in-law sitting with arms crossed.\n\n**Neurological**: T8 ASIA A — unchanged from baseline. Upper extremities 5/5 throughout. No motor or sensory function below T8. Intact sensation above T8.\n\n**Obstetric**: Fundal height appropriate for 20 weeks (at umbilicus). Fetal heart tones 148 bpm by Doppler. No vaginal bleeding or discharge.\n\n**Musculoskeletal**: Good upper body strength. Able to perform depression transfers independently. Shoulders — no impingement signs. Sitting balance excellent.\n\n**Skin**: No pressure injuries. Wheelchair cushion assessed — ROHO cushion with appropriate inflation. Ischial skin intact bilaterally. Skin over sacrum intact.\n\n**Respiratory**: Chest expansion symmetric. Forced vital capacity not measured today but was 85% predicted 6 months ago.\n\n**Functional**: Independent in all wheelchair-level ADLs. Demonstrates ability to transfer to exam table independently. Reports increasing difficulty with floor-to-wheelchair transfers as abdomen grows.',
